This namelist runs the dfmm verification gates (doc/dfmm_3d.md Sec. 7).
Compile using:
  cd bin && make COMPILER=METAL NDIM=3 HYDRO=1 DFMM=1 INIT=DFMMTEST   (stage 1)
  cd bin && make COMPILER=METAL NDIM=3 HYDRO=1 DFMM=2 INIT=DFMMTEST   (stage 2)
  cd bin && make COMPILER=METAL NDIM=3 HYDRO=1 DFMM=3 INIT=DFMMTEST   (stage 3)
  cd bin && make COMPILER=METAL NDIM=3 HYDRO=1 DFMM=4 INIT=DFMMTEST   (stage 4)

ALWAYS run 'make clean' when changing INIT= or DFMM=.  The Makefile does not
treat either as a dependency of condinit.o, so without it the binary silently
keeps the previous problem's initial condition.

Uniform p=1 with a divergence-free shear layer u_x = V0 sin(2 pi z / L), an
optional initial pressure anisotropy Pi_xx = A, Pi_yy = Pi_zz = -A/2, and an
optional isobaric density perturbation rho = 1 + D sin(2 pi z / L).

  Gate 2 (relaxation):    dfmm_ic_shear=0.0  dfmm_ic_pi=0.1  dfmm_tau=0.05
                          -> |Pi| must decay as exp(-t/tau)
  Gate 3 (NS limit):      dfmm_ic_shear=0.1  dfmm_ic_pi=0.0  dfmm_tau=1e-4
                          -> |Pi|/p -> 2 p tau |S0|, and |Pi-Pi_NS| -> 0
  Gate 4 (collisionless): dfmm_ic_shear=0.5  dfmm_ic_pi=0.0  dfmm_tau=-1.0
                          -> must stay realizable, min lam(P)/p > 0
  Gate 5 (Fourier limit,  dfmm_ic_drho=0.1   dfmm_tau=1e-4
          stage 2 only)   dfmm_prandtl=0.6666666666666667
                          -> q_z -> -(5/2) tau_q p d_z theta with
                             tau_q = tau/Pr, and |q-q_CE| -> 0

  Gate 6 (uniform advect,  dfmm_ic_uadv=0.3   dfmm_tau=-1.0   tout=0.2
          stage 3-4)       -> a flow with no velocity gradient, so everything
                              has a closed form:
                                D_i    = -uadv t
                                Sxv_ij = theta t delta_ij
                                Sxx_ij = (sigma_x0^2 + theta t^2) delta_ij
                                g      = sigma_x0/sqrt(sigma_x0^2 + theta t^2)
                              and |rho/detJ-1| = 0, max sig(dL/dx) = 1.
                              Read the fields from the snapshot; the run log
                              only carries the reduced diagnostics.

  Gate 7 (frozen shear,    dfmm_ic_shear=0.01  dfmm_tau=-1.0  tout=0.037
          stage 4)         dfmm_source=.false.
                          -> with the closure production off, Pi and Q stay at
                             zero, so Svv = theta I exactly and the velocity
                             field u_x = V0 sin(2 pi z) is a steady solution.
                             That isolates the -Sxv G^T term:
                               Sxv_zx = -g theta t^2/2,  Sxx_xz = -g theta t^3/6
                             with g = V0 [sin(k(z+dx))-sin(k(z-dx))]/(2dx), the
                             code's own centred difference.  Sxv_xz, Sxv_xy and
                             Sxx_xy must be identically zero.
                             Keep t k c_s < ~0.3 so the numerical damping of
                             the shear stays below the signal, and compare
                             against the discrete sums, not the continuum
                             limit -- the O(1/N) difference is not small at
                             these step counts.

  Gate 8 (diffusive limit, dfmm_ic_uadv=0.3   dfmm_tau=0.01   tout=0.5
          stage 4)         -> t >> tau, so the AP map must reach
                               Sxv -> tau theta,
                               Sxx -> sigma_x0^2 + 2 tau theta (t - tau)
                             i.e. Brownian spreading at D = tau theta = nu.
                             This is the gate that distinguishes the AP map
                             from the reference's post-source decay, which
                             would give Sxv -> 0 instead.

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
ncontrol=1
nrestart=0
nremap=0
nsubcycle=10*1
verbose=.false.
nstepmax=12
nsuperoct=2
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=4
levelmax=4
ngridtot=400000
ncachemax=200000
nexpand=1
boxlen=1.0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
nregion=1
region_type(1)='square'
x_center=0.5
y_center=0.5
z_center=0.5
length_x=10.0
length_y=10.0
length_z=10.0
exp_region=10.0
d_region=1.0
u_region=0.0
v_region=0.0
w_region=0.0
p_region=1.0
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
foutput=0
tout=0.3
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.6666666666666667
courant_factor=0.8
slope_type=1
riemann='hll'
/

&DFMM_PARAMS
dfmm_tau=1e-4
dfmm_prandtl=0.6666666666666667
dfmm_source=.true.
dfmm_diag=.true.
dfmm_ic_shear=0.1
dfmm_ic_pi=0.0
dfmm_ic_drho=0.0
dfmm_ic_uadv=0.0
dfmm_ic_sigmax=0.02
/
